{
 "kind": "app",
 "topic": "世界で最も権威あるIQテスト(ウェクスラー式など)の構造(下位検査・指標得点・合成得点・パーセンタイル・分類表・結果レポート)だけを真似し、中身は超馬鹿馬鹿しい問題と指標にした、受けられる体験型IQテスト。いちばん大事なのは、IQという数値を信じるに値しない理由や、それで人を判断してはいけない理由を何個も何個も挙げて示すこと。最後に受けた人へ『IQ』を数値で提示し、人を数値化して提示することの愚かさを示す。",
 "slug": "systems/nonsense-iq-test",
 "created": "2026-11-18",
 "engines": [
  "claude"
 ],
 "title": "The Extremely Authoritative Nonsense IQ Test",
 "tagline": "A serious-looking IQ test with absurd subtests that ends by showing why a single number can't sum you up.",
 "lead": "Take the EANIS-4½, a parody intelligence scale that copies only the format of the big professional tests: subtests, index scores, percentiles, classifications and an official report. The questions are ridiculous on purpose. Between subtests, and at the end, you get real reasons why an IQ number deserves skepticism and should never be used to judge anyone's worth.",
 "how_to_use": [
  "Press Begin Assessment and optionally enter a name for your official report.",
  "Answer the 14 absurd items across 7 subtests using mouse, touch or keyboard.",
  "Read the Psychometric Footnotes between subtests. They are the actual point.",
  "Reveal your Full Scale IQ, then use the experiment buttons to watch the same you get many different numbers."
 ],
 "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>EANIS-4½ · Extremely Authoritative Nonsense Intelligence Scale</title>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#f6f3ea;--paper:#fffdf7;--ink:#1d2330;--muted:#5b6272;--line:#d9d2bf;--accent:#1f4e8c;--accent2:#9c2f2f;--ok:#2f7a4a;--hl:#fff1b8;--shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.08)}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:#14171d;--paper:#1d212a;--ink:#e8e6df;--muted:#a3a9b6;--line:#353b48;--accent:#7fb0ff;--accent2:#ff8f8f;--ok:#78d39a;--hl:#4a4320;--shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.4)}}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\nbody{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:16px 14px 60px}\nh1,h2,h3{font-family:Georgia,\"Times New Roman\",serif;line-height:1.2;margin:.2em 0 .5em}\nh1{font-size:1.6rem}h2{font-size:1.3rem}h3{font-size:1.05rem}\n.paper{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);padding:18px;margin:14px 0}\n.masthead{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;border-bottom:3px double var(--line);padding-bottom:12px;margin-bottom:6px}\n.seal{flex:0 0 64px;height:64px;border-radius:50%;border:3px double var(--accent);display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:30px;color:var(--accent)}\n.small{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.caps{font-variant:small-caps;letter-spacing:.06em}\nbutton{font:inherit;cursor:pointer;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);padding:10px 14px;min-height:44px}\nbutton:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}\nbutton:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,[tabindex]:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}\n.primary{background:var(--accent);color:var(--paper);border-color:var(--accent);font-weight:600}\n.primary:hover{filter:brightness(1.1)}\n.opts{display:grid;gap:10px;margin-top:12px}\n.opts button{text-align:left}\n.row{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}\n.bar{height:8px;background:var(--line);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}\n.bar>i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--accent);width:0;transition:width .3s}\n.matrix{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,64px);gap:6px;justify-content:center;margin:12px 0}\n.matrix span{display:grid;place-items:center;height:64px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;font-size:30px;background:var(--bg)}\n.big-emoji{font-size:44px;text-align:center;margin:10px 0;min-height:66px;letter-spacing:.15em}\n.keys{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr);gap:6px;margin-top:12px}\n.keys button{font-size:24px;padding:6px 0}\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem}\nth,td{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:7px 6px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}\nth{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:600}\ntd.n,th.n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\ntr.hit td{background:var(--hl);font-weight:600}\n.scroll{overflow-x:auto}\n.reason{border-left:4px solid var(--accent);padding:8px 12px;margin:10px 0;background:var(--bg);border-radius:0 6px 6px 0}\n.reason b{display:block}\n.reason.ours{border-left-color:var(--accent2)}\n.counter{display:inline-block;background:var(--accent2);color:var(--paper);border-radius:999px;padding:2px 10px;font-size:.8rem;font-weight:700}\n.iq{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(4rem,20vw,7rem);text-align:center;line-height:1;margin:10px 0 0;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--accent)}\n.stamp{display:inline-block;border:3px solid var(--accent2);color:var(--accent2);padding:4px 10px;transform:rotate(-4deg);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.85rem}\n.exp{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:8px;margin:12px 0}\n.hist{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-weight:600;word-break:break-word}\ninput[type=text]{font:inherit;padding:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);width:100%;max-width:340px}\ninput[type=range]{width:100%;accent-color:var(--accent2)}\ndetails summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;padding:6px 0}\n.center{text-align:center}\n[hidden]{display:none!important}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{transition:none!important}}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main>\n<header class=\"masthead\">\n  <div class=\"seal\" aria-hidden=\"true\">🧠</div>\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"caps small\">Official Psychometric Instrument · Form B-ish</div>\n    <h1 style=\"margin:0\">EANIS-4½</h1>\n    <div class=\"small\">Extremely Authoritative Nonsense Intelligence Scale, Fourth-and-a-Half Edition</div>\n  </div>\n</header>\n<p class=\"small\">A parody. It copies only the <em>format</em> of professional intelligence tests. It is not a real assessment, and nothing on this page measures you. <span class=\"counter\" id=\"rc\" aria-live=\"polite\">0 reasons shown</span></p>\n\n<section id=\"intro\" class=\"screen paper\">\n  <h2 tabindex=\"-1\" data-focus>Examiner's Manual, Page 1</h2>\n  <p>Welcome, Examinee. You are about to complete <b>7 subtests</b> combined into <b>4 index scores</b> and one <b>Full Scale Intelligence-ish Quotient</b>, complete with percentiles, a classification table and an official report.</p>\n  <p>The questions are absurd. The scoring is arbitrary. In other words, the format is the only real thing here. That format is exactly what makes a number look trustworthy.</p>\n  <p>Between subtests you will receive <b>Psychometric Footnotes</b>: real reasons an IQ score should be read with caution and never used to rank a person's worth. Please read them. They are the actual test.</p>\n  <label for=\"nm\" class=\"small\">Examinee name for the official report (optional, stays on this page)</label><br>\n  <input type=\"text\" id=\"nm\" maxlength=\"40\" placeholder=\"e.g. A. Person\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n  <div class=\"row\" style=\"margin-top:14px\"><button class=\"primary\" id=\"begin\">Begin Assessment</button><span class=\"small\">About 4 minutes. No time pressure, except where the test is pretending.</span></div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"test\" class=\"screen paper\" hidden>\n  <div class=\"row\" style=\"justify-content:space-between\"><span class=\"caps small\" id=\"sc\"></span><span class=\"small\" id=\"inum\"></span></div>\n  <div class=\"bar\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i id=\"prog\"></i></div>\n  <h2 id=\"sn\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-focus style=\"margin-top:12px\"></h2>\n  <p class=\"small\" id=\"si\"></p>\n  <p class=\"small\" id=\"sx\" style=\"font-style:italic\"></p>\n  <h3 id=\"q\"></h3>\n  <div id=\"vis\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>\n  <div id=\"opts\" class=\"opts\"></div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"inter\" class=\"screen paper\" hidden>\n  <div class=\"caps small\">Mandatory Pause</div>\n  <h2 tabindex=\"-1\" data-focus id=\"ih\">Psychometric Footnotes</h2>\n  <p class=\"small\">Before the test continues, please consider the following. Unlike the questions, these points are real.</p>\n  <div id=\"ir\"></div>\n  <button class=\"primary\" id=\"icont\" style=\"margin-top:8px\">Continue</button>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"report\" class=\"screen\" hidden>\n  <div class=\"paper\">\n    <div class=\"row\" style=\"justify-content:space-between\"><div class=\"caps small\">Score Report · Confidential-ish</div><span class=\"stamp\">Not a real test</span></div>\n    <h2 tabindex=\"-1\" data-focus>Official Results Report</h2>\n    <p class=\"small\" id=\"rmeta\"></p>\n    <h3>Subtest Scaled Scores</h3>\n    <p class=\"small\">Scaled scores run from 1 to 19 with a mean of 10. Ours include deliberately added random noise. Real tests don't add noise on purpose, but every measurement contains some.</p>\n    <div class=\"scroll\"><table id=\"tsub\"></table></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"paper\">\n    <h3>Index Scores</h3>\n    <p class=\"small\">Index scores use a mean of 100 and an SD of 15, like many real tests. The percentile says what share of an imaginary norm group you outscored. Our norm group has zero members.</p>\n    <div class=\"scroll\"><table id=\"tidx\"></table></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"paper center\">\n    <h3>Full Scale Intelligence-ish Quotient</h3>\n    <p class=\"small\">Seven subtests and fourteen silly questions, combined into one number.</p>\n    <button class=\"primary\" id=\"reveal\">Reveal my IQ</button>\n    <div id=\"fs\" hidden>\n      <div class=\"iq\" id=\"iqn\" aria-live=\"polite\">0</div>\n      <p id=\"iqc\" style=\"font-weight:600;margin:.3em 0\"></p>\n      <p class=\"small\" id=\"iqp\"></p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"after\" hidden>\n    <div class=\"paper\">\n      <h3>Classification Table</h3>\n      <p class=\"small\">Every label below describes the test or the situation, never the person. Real classification labels have been rewritten many times, for good reason.</p>\n      <div class=\"scroll\"><table id=\"tcls\"></table></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"paper\">\n      <h2>Experiment: Is That Number Solid?</h2>\n      <p>Your answers stay the same. Only the scoring assumptions change. Press the buttons and watch the number move.</p>\n      <div class=\"exp\">\n        <button data-x=\"old\">Score me against older norms</button>\n        <button data-x=\"grp\">Swap the norm group</button>\n        <button data-x=\"prac\">Retake after practice</button>\n        <button data-x=\"sleep\">Take it after a bad night's sleep</button>\n        <button data-x=\"wt\">Re-weight the index scores</button>\n        <button data-x=\"ci\">Show the confidence interval</button>\n        <button data-x=\"orig\">Back to original score</button>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"paper\" style=\"margin:0;background:var(--bg)\">\n        <div class=\"iq\" id=\"xn\" style=\"font-size:3.4rem\">–</div>\n        <p id=\"xw\" class=\"small center\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n        <p class=\"small\">Numbers assigned to the same unchanged you:</p>\n        <p class=\"hist\" id=\"xh\"></p>\n        <p id=\"xs\" style=\"font-weight:600\"></p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"paper\">\n      <h2>Why You Shouldn't Trust This Number (or Any Single IQ Number) to Judge a Person</h2>\n      <p>All of the reasons, gathered in one place. The first five groups apply to real, professionally built tests. The last group applies to this one.</p>\n      <div id=\"allr\"></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"paper\">\n      <h3>One Last Measurement</h3>\n      <label for=\"worth\">How much does this number say about your worth as a person?</label>\n      <input type=\"range\" id=\"worth\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" value=\"0\" aria-describedby=\"wo\">\n      <p id=\"wo\" aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"small\">0%. Correct.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"paper\">\n      <h2>Final Interpretation</h2>\n      <p>You were just handed a number with three digits, a percentile, a classification and an official-looking stamp. It came from questions about socks, pancakes and pigeons. It still probably felt like it meant something for a second.</p>\n      <p><b>That feeling is the point.</b> Turning a person into a number makes a complicated, changing human look simple, fixed and rankable. Real IQ tests are carefully built tools. In skilled hands they can answer narrow questions, like whether a child needs a particular kind of support. They are not verdicts on who someone is, what they deserve, or what they will become.</p>\n      <p>Whatever number you got: you are more than it, and so is everyone else.</p>\n      <button id=\"again\">Take the test again (and get a different number)</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n</main>\n\n<script>\n(function(){\n\"use strict\";\nvar $=function(s){return document.querySelector(s)};\nvar R=Math.random;\nfunction shuffle(a){a=a.slice();for(var i=a.length-1;i>0;i--){var j=Math.floor(R()*(i+1));var t=a[i];a[i]=a[j];a[j]=t}return a}\nfunction el(tag,attrs,text){var e=document.createElement(tag);if(attrs)for(var k in attrs)e.setAttribute(k,attrs[k]);if(text!=null)e.textContent=text;return e}\nvar reduce=window.matchMedia&&matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;\n\nvar IDX={\n VOI:{name:'Verbal Overthinking Index',sub:[0,1]},\n FNI:{name:'Fluid Napping Index',sub:[2,3]},\n WFI:{name:'Working Forgetting Index',sub:[4]},\n PSI:{name:'Processing Slowness Index',sub:[5,6]}\n};\nfunction mtx(cells){return '<div class=\"matrix\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pattern grid: '+cells.join(', ')+'\">'+cells.map(function(c){return '<span aria-hidden=\"true\">'+c+'</span>'}).join('')+'</div>'}\n\nvar SUB=[\n {name:'Snack Similarities',idx:'VOI',instr:'Explain how two things are alike. Answer as you would to a very serious examiner holding a clipboard.',\n  aside:'Parody of a verbal reasoning subtest. Real versions use open answers that an examiner scores by judgment.',\n  items:[\n  {q:'In what way are a SOCK and a PANCAKE alike?',opts:[['Both are best served warm',2],['Both disappear mysteriously',1],['Both are flat if you believe hard enough',2],['They are not alike, and that is their right',1]]},\n  {q:'In what way are a CLOUD and a CAT alike?',opts:[['Both sit wherever they want',2],['Both are fluffy and indifferent to you',2],['Both can rain on your parade',1],['Neither returns emails',0]]}]},\n {name:'Vocabulary of Vibes',idx:'VOI',instr:'Define each word. Precision is optional. Vibes are mandatory.',\n  aside:'Vocabulary tasks reward exposure to a particular language and schooling, not only reasoning.',\n  items:[\n  {q:'Define the word \"TUESDAY\".',opts:[['A Monday that has given up',2],['The day after Monday, in most calendars',1],['A vibe, not a day',2],['I would rather not',0]]},\n  {q:'Define the word \"SNACK\".',opts:[['A meal with no commitment',2],['Food eaten between meals',1],['A small treat that becomes four',2],['A lifestyle',1]]}]},\n {name:'Nap Matrices',idx:'FNI',instr:'Find the item that best completes the pattern. The most logical answer is not always worth the most points. Welcome to psychometrics.',\n  aside:'Pattern-completion tasks are often called \"culture-fair\". Average scores on them still rose a lot across the 20th century.',\n  items:[\n  {q:'Which item completes the grid?',visual:mtx(['☀️','😐','🌙','☀️','😑','🌙','☀️','😴','❓']),opts:[['🌙 Moon (the logical answer)',1],['🛌 Bed',2],['☕ Coffee',0],['🦉 Owl',2]]},\n  {q:'Which item completes the grid?',visual:mtx(['🥚','🐣','🐥','🌰','🌱','❓','💧','☁️','🌧️']),opts:[['🌳 Tree (the logical answer)',1],['🌷 Tulip',1],['🍕 Pizza (ambition)',2],['🌰 Back to the start',2]]}]},\n {name:'Couch Design',idx:'FNI',instr:'Mentally manipulate furniture. Do not physically manipulate furniture.',\n  aside:'Parody of a spatial construction subtest. Real ones are often timed, so speed sneaks into the score.',\n  items:[\n  {q:'If you rotate this couch 90° clockwise, what do you get?',visual:'<div class=\"big-emoji\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"a couch\">🛋️</div>',opts:[['A vertical couch',1],['A very bad night of sleep',2],['An argument with movers',2],['Still a couch, emotionally',1]]},\n  {q:'How many more cushions fit on a couch that is already full of cushions?',opts:[['Zero',1],['One more. Always one more.',2],['Infinitely many',1],['Depends who is asking',2]]}]},\n {name:'Pigeon Span',idx:'WFI',instr:'A sequence appears for about 3 seconds. Remember it. Pigeons are watching.',\n  aside:'This index rests on a single subtest. Fewer items mean less reliability, in real tests too.',\n  items:[\n  {q:'Which sequence did you see, in the same order?',type:'memory',seq:['🐦','🍞','🐦','🎩'],\n   opts:[['🐦 🍞 🐦 🎩',2],['🐦 🐦 🍞 🎩',1],['🍞 🐦 🎩 🐦',1],['🎩 🐦 🍞 🐦',1]]},\n  {q:'Which is the sequence you saw, but BACKWARDS?',type:'memory',seq:['🍌','🦆','🎺'],\n   opts:[['🎺 🦆 🍌',2],['🍌 🦆 🎺',1],['🦆 🎺 🍌',1],['🎺 🍌 🦆',1]]}]},\n {name:'Processing Slowness',idx:'PSI',instr:'In this subtest, patience is speed. Probably.',\n  aside:'Real processing speed tasks reward going fast. Here we reward going slow. Both choices are equally made up.',\n  items:[\n  {q:'Press the button below as SLOWLY as you can bear. Waiting earns points.',type:'slow'},\n  {q:'Find the lost key 🔑 among the household items and select it.',type:'keys'}]}\n];\n// split PSI into two subtests so we have 7\nSUB.splice(6,0,{name:'Symbol Search for Lost Keys',idx:'PSI',instr:'Locate the key. Points are awarded for taking just long enough to appreciate each item.',aside:'Timed search tasks can penalize anyone with visual, motor or attention differences, regardless of reasoning.',items:[SUB[5].items[1],{q:'Find the lost key 🔑 again. It moved. Keys do that.',type:'keys'}]});\nSUB[5].items=[SUB[5].items[0],{q:'One more time. Press as SLOWLY as you can. The examiner is pretending not to watch.',type:'slow'}];\n\nvar REASONS=[\n ['Measurement','Every score is an estimate','Even well-built professional tests report scores with a confidence interval, often several points either way. A single number hides that blur.'],\n ['Measurement','Same person, different day','Sleep, illness, stress, hunger, pain and motivation can all shift performance on any given day.'],\n ['Measurement','Practice changes the score','Taking the same or a similar test again usually raises scores somewhat. That is one reason professionals avoid retesting too soon.'],\n ['Measurement','It is a rank, not a quantity','An IQ score is a position compared against a norm group. Change the group, or the year it was collected, and the same answers get a different number.'],\n ['Measurement','The yardstick drifts over time','In many countries, average raw test performance rose substantially during the 20th century (the \"Flynn effect\"), often cited at around 3 points per decade. In some countries the trend has recently slowed or reversed. Tests must be re-normed, so a \"100\" from one era is not a \"100\" from another.'],\n ['Measurement','Extremes are the least precise','Very high and very low scores rest on few people in the norm sample, so they are estimated less precisely than scores near the middle.'],\n ['Measurement','Human judgment is built in','Some subtests require an examiner to score open-ended answers. Research has documented administration and scoring errors, even among trained examiners.'],\n ['Measurement','One average can hide a lumpy profile','When a person\\'s index scores differ a lot, the full-scale average may describe a pattern of strengths they don\\'t actually have.'],\n ['Context','Language and familiarity matter','Items assume familiarity with a particular language, style of schooling and kind of content. Less familiarity can lower a score without meaning less ability.'],\n ['Context','School changes the score','Research suggests that additional years of education are associated with gains in measured IQ. The number partly reflects opportunity.'],\n ['Context','Environment leaves fingerprints','Nutrition, exposure to toxins such as lead, chronic stress and poverty are all associated with test scores. A score carries a person\\'s circumstances along with them.'],\n ['Context','Speed is not depth','Timed tasks reward working fast. A careful, thorough thinker can lose points for exactly that carefulness.'],\n ['Context','Bodies and senses differ','Vision, hearing, motor or attention differences can lower scores on tasks not designed with that person in mind. This is why accommodations and careful interpretation matter.'],\n ['Context','The testing room is never neutral','Test anxiety, comfort with the examiner and awareness of stereotypes may affect performance. Research on \"stereotype threat\" is debated, but nobody takes a test in a vacuum.'],\n ['Context','Scores can change','Especially in childhood and adolescence, a person\\'s measured IQ can shift meaningfully over the years. It is a snapshot, not a tattoo.'],\n ['What it leaves out','Huge parts of a mind are missing','Creativity, kindness, wisdom, humor, courage, craftsmanship and judgment in real situations are not what these tests measure.'],\n ['What it leaves out','Effort and curiosity are invisible','Persistence, curiosity and the willingness to keep learning shape lives enormously. A one-sitting test doesn\\'t capture them.'],\n ['What it leaves out','Understanding people is not on the menu','Reading a room, comforting a friend and resolving a conflict are skills of their own, and the test leaves them out.'],\n ['What it leaves out','Prediction is about crowds, not you','IQ scores correlate with some outcomes on average across large groups, but individuals vary enormously. A score can\\'t tell you what one particular person will do.'],\n ['What it leaves out','Averages say nothing about the person in front of you','Statistics about any group, however they are defined, cannot tell you about an individual. Judging a person by a group average is a reasoning error.'],\n ['What it leaves out','It was built as one tool among many','Professionals use these tests together with interviews, history and observation to answer specific questions, such as identifying learning needs. They were never meant as a measure of human value.'],\n ['History & ethics','Even an early creator warned against this','Alfred Binet co-created an early intelligence scale to identify schoolchildren who needed extra support. He cautioned against treating it as a measure of fixed, innate intelligence.'],\n ['History & ethics','The numbers have been used to hurt people','In the early 20th century, intelligence test results were used to support eugenic policies, including forced sterilization laws in several countries and arguments for restricting immigration.'],\n ['History & ethics','The categories are conventions','Classification labels have been revised many times. Terms once printed in official manuals are now recognized as insults. The categories were invented by people, not discovered in nature.'],\n ['History & ethics','Labels stick','A number can shape how teachers, employers and the person themselves see their potential. How large that effect is remains debated, but it is reason enough for caution.'],\n ['History & ethics','Objective-looking is not objective','People chose which tasks to include, how to weight them, which norm group to use and what to call the results. A number can carry all of those choices while looking neutral.'],\n ['History & ethics','Online \"IQ tests\" are mostly unvalidated','Most quick online IQ tests have no proper norms or validation research behind them. That includes, proudly, this one.'],\n ['This test','The norm sample is imaginary','Your percentile compares you with nobody. It was computed from a bell curve we simply assumed.'],\n ['This test','Points were assigned by vibes','The \"correct\" answers were chosen by gut feeling, and the logical answer sometimes scored lower. Real tests are far more careful, yet someone still decides what counts as correct.'],\n ['This test','Random noise is added on purpose','Each scaled score gets random noise, and the full scale score gets an extra \"examiner mood\" adjustment. Retake the test and see.'],\n ['This test','It took four minutes','A few minutes of answers were turned into a three-digit verdict. Any single sitting is a thin slice of a person.']\n];\nvar shownR=0;\nfunction bumpR(n){shownR=Math.max(shownR,n);$('#rc').textContent=shownR+' reason'+(shownR===1?'':'s')+' shown';}\nfunction reasonNode(r){var d=el('div',{'class':'reason'+(r[0]==='This test'?' ours':'')});d.appendChild(el('b',null,r[1]));d.appendChild(el('span',null,r[2]));return d}\n\nvar CLS=[[130,'Test Was Clearly Too Easy'],[120,'Probably Had Coffee'],[110,'Read the Questions Suspiciously Well'],[90,'Statistically Typical Human (Excellent)'],[80,'Probably Hungry'],[70,'Test Was Too Weird for the Moment'],[-999,'The Test Failed You, Not the Other Way Round']];\nfunction cls(v){for(var i=0;i<CLS.length;i++)if(v>=CLS[i][0])return i;return CLS.length-1}\n\nvar s=0,i=0,raw=[],total=0,done=0,timer=null;\nSUB.forEach(function(st){total+=st.items.length});\n\nfunction show(id){document.querySelectorAll('.screen').forEach(function(e){e.hidden=e.id!==id});window.scrollTo(0,0);var f=document.querySelector('#'+id+' [data-focus]');if(f)f.focus({preventScroll:true});}\n\nfunction start(){s=0;i=0;done=0;raw=SUB.map(function(){return 0});show('test');renderItem();}\n\nfunction renderItem(){\n  clearTimeout(timer);\n  var st=SUB[s],it=st.items[i];\n  $('#sc').textContent='Subtest '+(s+1)+' of '+SUB.length+' · '+IDX[st.idx].name;\n  $('#inum').textContent='Item '+(i+1)+' of '+st.items.length;\n  $('#prog').style.width=(done/total*100)+'%';\n  $('#sn').textContent=st.name;$('#si').textContent=st.instr;$('#sx').textContent=st.aside;\n  $('#q').textContent=it.q;\n  var vis=$('#vis'),opts=$('#opts');vis.innerHTML=it.visual||'';opts.innerHTML='';\n  if(it.type==='memory'){\n    var b=el('button',{'class':'primary'},'Show the sequence (about 3 seconds)');\n    b.onclick=function(){\n      opts.innerHTML='';\n      var box=el('div',{'class':'big-emoji','aria-label':'Sequence: '+it.seq.join(' ')},it.seq.join(' '));\n      vis.innerHTML='';vis.appendChild(box);\n      timer=setTimeout(function(){box.textContent='🙈';box.setAttribute('aria-label','Sequence hidden. Choose an answer.');renderOpts(it.opts)},3000);\n    };\n    opts.appendChild(b);\n  }else if(it.type==='slow'){\n    var t0=performance.now(),bs=el('button',{'class':'primary'},'Press me… slowly');\n    var hint=el('p',{'class':'small'},'Tip: real speed tests would be scoring you right now. This one is waiting.');\n    bs.onclick=function(){var t=(performance.now()-t0)/1000;answer(t<3?0:t<8?1:2)};\n    opts.appendChild(bs);opts.appendChild(hint);\n  }else if(it.type==='keys'){\n    var pool=['🧦','🥄','🧸','📎','🪥','🧽','🕶️','🧤','🔋','🪀','🧯','📦','🥢','🧻','🪒','🎈','🧲','🪣','🧷','🖍️','🎲','🧴','📌'];\n    var cells=shuffle(pool).slice(0,23);cells.push('🔑');cells=shuffle(cells);\n    var g=el('div',{'class':'keys',role:'group','aria-label':'Household items grid'});var tk=performance.now();\n    cells.forEach(function(c,n){var kb=el('button',{'aria-label':'Item '+(n+1)+(c==='🔑'?': key':': not a key, probably')},c);\n      kb.onclick=function(){if(c!=='🔑'){kb.disabled=true;kb.textContent='·';return}var t=(performance.now()-tk)/1000;answer(t<2?1:t<7?2:1)};g.appendChild(kb)});\n    opts.appendChild(g);\n  }else renderOpts(it.opts);\n  $('#sn').focus({preventScroll:true});\n}\nfunction renderOpts(list){\n  var opts=$('#opts');opts.innerHTML='';\n  shuffle(list).forEach(function(o){var b=el('button',null,o[0]);b.onclick=function(){answer(o[1])};opts.appendChild(b)});\n}\nfunction answer(p){\n  clearTimeout(timer);raw[s]+=p;done++;i++;\n  if(i>=SUB[s].items.length)interlude();else renderItem();\n}\nfunction interlude(){\n  var per=4,from=s*per,list=REASONS.slice(from,from+per),box=$('#ir');box.innerHTML='';\n  list.forEach(function(r){box.appendChild(reasonNode(r))});\n  bumpR(Math.min(REASONS.length,from+per));\n  $('#ih').textContent='Psychometric Footnotes · after Subtest '+(s+1);\n  $('#icont').textContent=s<SUB.length-1?'Continue to Subtest '+(s+2)+': '+SUB[s+1].name:'Generate my Official Report';\n  show('inter');\n}\n$('#icont').onclick=function(){s++;i=0;if(s<SUB.length){show('test');renderItem()}else report()};\n\nfunction erf(x){var t=1/(1+.3275911*Math.abs(x)),y=1-(((((1.061405429*t-1.453152027)*t)+1.421413741)*t-.284496736)*t+.254829592)*t*Math.exp(-x*x);return x>=0?y:-y}\nfunction pct(v){var p=50*(1+erf((v-100)/15/Math.SQRT2));p=Math.min(99.9,Math.max(.1,p));return p<1||p>99?p.toFixed(1):String(Math.round(p))}\nfunction ord(p){var n=parseFloat(p);if(String(p).indexOf('.')>-1)return p+'th';var k=n%100;if(k>10&&k<14)return p+'th';return p+(['th','st','nd','rd'][n%10]||'th')}\n\nvar scaled=[],idxS={},base=0,hist=[];\nfunction report(){\n  scaled=raw.map(function(r){return Math.max(1,Math.min(19,Math.round(5+r*2.6+(R()*4-2))))});\n  var nm=$('#nm').value.trim()||'Anonymous Examinee';\n  $('#rmeta').textContent='Examinee: '+nm+' · Date: '+new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US',{year:'numeric',month:'long',day:'numeric'})+' · Examiner: a JavaScript file';\n  var t=$('#tsub');t.innerHTML='<thead><tr><th>Subtest</th><th>Index</th><th class=\"n\">Raw</th><th class=\"n\">Scaled</th></tr></thead>';\n  var tb=el('tbody');\n  SUB.forEach(function(st,n){var tr=el('tr');tr.appendChild(el('td',null,st.name));tr.appendChild(el('td',null,st.idx));tr.appendChild(el('td',{'class':'n'},raw[n]+'/4'));tr.appendChild(el('td',{'class':'n'},scaled[n]));tb.appendChild(tr)});\n  t.appendChild(tb);\n  var ti=$('#tidx');ti.innerHTML='<thead><tr><th>Index</th><th class=\"n\">Score</th><th class=\"n\">Percentile</th><th class=\"n\">95% CI*</th></tr></thead>';\n  var ib=el('tbody');\n  Object.keys(IDX).forEach(function(k){\n    var sub=IDX[k].sub,m=sub.reduce(function(a,b){return a+scaled[b]},0)/sub.length;\n    var v=Math.round(100+(m-10)*5.5);idxS[k]=v;\n    var tr=el('tr');tr.appendChild(el('td',null,IDX[k].name+' ('+k+')'+(sub.length===1?' · based on one subtest':'')));\n    tr.appendChild(el('td',{'class':'n'},v));tr.appendChild(el('td',{'class':'n'},ord(pct(v))));tr.appendChild(el('td',{'class':'n'},(v-8)+'–'+(v+8)));ib.appendChild(tr)});\n  ti.appendChild(ib);\n  var cap=el('caption',{'class':'small',style:'caption-side:bottom;text-align:left;padding-top:6px'},'*Illustrative band. Real tests publish confidence intervals because no score is exact. Ours is made up, like everything else here.');ti.appendChild(cap);\n  var mAll=scaled.reduce(function(a,b){return a+b},0)/scaled.length;\n  base=Math.round(100+(mAll-10)*5.8+(R()*6-3));\n  hist=[];$('#fs').hidden=true;$('#after').hidden=true;$('#reveal').hidden=false;\n  var tc=$('#tcls');tc.innerHTML='<thead><tr><th>Score range</th><th>EANIS classification</th></tr></thead>';\n  var cb=el('tbody'),hit=cls(base);\n  CLS.forEach(function(c,n){var hi=n===0?'130+':(c[0]<0?'Below 70':c[0]+'–'+(CLS[n-1][0]-1));var tr=el('tr',n===hit?{'class':'hit'}:null);tr.appendChild(el('td',null,hi));tr.appendChild(el('td',null,c[1]+(n===hit?'  ← you, allegedly':'')));cb.appendChild(tr)});\n  tc.appendChild(cb);\n  var all=$('#allr');all.innerHTML='';var cats=[];REASONS.forEach(function(r){if(cats.indexOf(r[0])<0)cats.push(r[0])});\n  var num=0;cats.forEach(function(c){var d=el('details');d.open=true;var items=REASONS.filter(function(r){return r[0]===c});\n    d.appendChild(el('summary',null,c+' ('+items.length+')'));items.forEach(function(r){num++;var n=reasonNode(r);n.firstChild.textContent=num+'. '+r[1];d.appendChild(n)});all.appendChild(d)});\n  $('#worth').value=0;$('#wo').textContent='0%. Correct.';\n  show('report');\n}\n$('#reveal').onclick=function(){\n  $('#reveal').hidden=true;$('#fs').hidden=false;\n  var n=$('#iqn'),c=CLS[cls(base)][1];\n  function fin(){n.textContent=base;$('#iqc').textContent='Classification: '+c;$('#iqp').textContent='Percentile: '+ord(pct(base))+' (compared with an imaginary norm group of zero people). Now please keep scrolling. The important part comes next.';$('#after').hidden=false;setX(base,'Original score, exactly as precise as it looked a moment ago.');bumpR(REASONS.length)}\n  if(reduce){fin();return}\n  var st=performance.now();(function f(){var k=Math.min(1,(performance.now()-st)/1400);n.textContent=Math.round(base*(1-Math.pow(1-k,3)));if(k<1)requestAnimationFrame(f);else fin()})();\n};\nfunction setX(v,why){v=Math.round(v);hist.push(v);$('#xn').textContent=v;$('#xw').textContent=why;$('#xh').textContent=hist.join(' → ');\n  var mn=Math.min.apply(null,hist),mx=Math.max.apply(null,hist);\n  $('#xs').textContent=hist.length<2?'':'Range so far: '+mn+' to '+mx+' ('+(mx-mn)+' points apart), from '+CLS[cls(mx)][1]+' to '+CLS[cls(mn)][1]+'. You did not change once.';}\ndocument.querySelectorAll('[data-x]').forEach(function(b){b.onclick=function(){\n  var x=b.getAttribute('data-x');\n  if(x==='old')setX(base+9,'Same answers, compared with norms collected about 30 years earlier. This illustrates the roughly 3-points-per-decade rise often cited for the 20th century. Older norms make everyone look \"smarter\".');\n  else if(x==='grp'){var d=Math.round(R()*16-8);if(d===0)d=5;setX(base+d,'Same answers, compared with a different (equally imaginary) group of people. Your rank changed by '+(d>0?'+':'')+d+'.')}\n  else if(x==='prac')setX(base+3+Math.round(R()*4),'Same you, a little more familiar with the format. Illustration of a practice effect.');\n  else if(x==='sleep')setX(base-3-Math.round(R()*7),'Same you, tired. Illustration of how a bad night can cost points.');\n  else if(x==='wt'){var ks=Object.keys(idxS),w=ks.map(function(){return .2+R()}),sw=w.reduce(function(a,b){return a+b},0),v=ks.reduce(function(a,k,n){return a+idxS[k]*w[n]},0)/sw;\n    setX(v,'Same index scores, different weights: '+ks.map(function(k,n){return k+' '+Math.round(w[n]/sw*100)+'%'}).join(', ')+'. Someone always picks the weights.')}\n  else if(x==='ci'){$('#xw').textContent='If this were a real test, the report might give a 95% confidence interval of about '+(base-6)+' to '+(base+6)+'. That means even the professionals don\\'t claim to know your \"true\" score to the point. And ours isn\\'t a real test.';}\n  else setX(base,'Back to the original number. It is no more \"real\" than the others.');\n};});\n$('#worth').addEventListener('input',function(){var w=this;if(+w.value>0){$('#wo').textContent=w.value+'%? No. Snapping back to 0%. A test score is not a measure of anyone\\'s worth.';setTimeout(function(){w.value=0},350)}else $('#wo').textContent='0%. Correct.'});\n$('#begin').onclick=start;\n$('#again').onclick=function(){show('intro')};\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>",
